From 14e1eba3e06fe1f5342f0e1b430f114efb1447ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:27:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): refuse notice-only hub rows as decision
 subscribers [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Review 5990038078 of #3730 @487100b0: has_chat_subscriber accepted every
well-formed platform=hub row, so a card whose only hub sub was touch or
send_refused parked and posted decision_requested. hermes-hub collect_tasks
and _counted_sub_clause exclude those UNCOUNTED_SUB_REASONS, so _linked_chats
was empty and the origin chat got 0 wakes.

Problem: a creator ask on a notice-only hub row parked silently with no
wakeable session.
Why 1: the hub branch returned True on a 3-part chat_id — evidence: review
probe on 487100b0 (scheduled, 1 decision_requested, sessions=[], 0 wakes).
Why 2: this PR admitted hub destinations without the publisher's counted
predicate — evidence: kanban_db_notify.UNCOUNTED_SUB_REASONS and
hermes_hub._task_subscriptions counted clause.
Why 3: the existing hub eligibility test seeded reason=shepherd only.
Root (happened): decision eligibility did not share the collector's
counted-sub predicate.
Root (not caught): no schedule-tool test whose only hub row was
send_refused or touch.
Recurrence: second fail-open in this PR (rollout re-notify was the first).

Countermeasures:
- symptom: hub branch of has_chat_subscriber skips touch/send_refused
- detection: test_notice_only_hub_row_is_not_a_decision_subscriber (RED on
  487100b0, 2 failed; GREEN after, 2 passed). Focused 9 files 215 passed.
  scripts/check --base origin/main 21 ok.
- cosmetics from the same review: drop the dead drop_mark(task) is None
  conjunct (ask envelopes are scheduled; drop_mark needs blocked) and the
  unused _terminal_states helper.

Mixed-version (an operator instruction point 2): INCOMPLETE. The hub notify row has
no advertised receiver core version or "reads ask_notice" capability
(chat_id is only gw/profile/session; replica meta has gateway/cursor/head).
No handshake added. A mixed-version window can still park unseen until the
receiver updates.

No change to who may answer an ask. Genuine human_request stays
user-directed.
